    "title": "Are supermarkets open on Easter Sunday? Depends where you shop. See the list",
    "text": "Credit: John Greim/LightRocket via Getty ImagesWhile big warehouse brands like Costco and Sam's Club are frequently releasing all-new items for their loyal shoppers, more traditional grocery stores like Publix and Walmart tend to do so less frequently—or at least, with much less fanfare. But Publix may have seen how popular these limited-edition releases are and decided they can play that game, too.In recent months, we've spotted a noticeable uptick in the number of Publix-exclusive \"limited-edition\" foods in the Florida-based grocery store's aisles. A few weeks ago, we found a new line of mini cream cheese pies had been quietly rolled out to the bakery, and of course, they've been thrilling customers who have a sweet tooth with all-new ice cream launches for a while.But savvy shoppers will notice that these new introductions are showing up in more aisles than ever before. Here, five new products we spotted at Publix this month, and since we don't know how long they'll be around, it's a good idea to grab them if and when you do run across any on your next trip.Unsweetened Peach Flavored Black TeaCredit: Kimberly Holland/Southern LivingPublix has stand-by favorites like sweet tea and lemonade always available, but in recent weeks, we've spotted a few other brand-new offerings, including Unsweetened Peach Flavored Black Tea (pictured), Peach Coconut Flavored Lemonade, and Honey Flavored Chamomile Ginger Herbal Tea. They're all in the refrigerated section of prepared foods, and most come in either ready-to-travel 20-ounce bottles or family-friendly half gallons.Chicken Parmigiana-Style DipCredit: Kimberly Holland/Southern LivingThis all-new dip certainly grabbed my attention when I first saw it. A chicken Parmesan-style dip? That's a first for me. But you'll find the new dip alongside Publix's array of party-ready appetizers and spreads. It's described as being made \"with cheese blend, marinara sauce, and garlic.\" Can't be too mad about that.Home Run Caramel Popcorn Premium Ice CreamCredit: Kimberly Holland/Southern LivingBoth of the ice creams in this picture are returning favorites, but keep your eyes open for their new flavors for spring and summer—Bavarian Crème Hot Honey Praline, Bourbon Praline Crumble, Peanut Butter & Jelly, and Root Beer Float. I haven't spotted them yet, but each time I go to the store, a new flavor has been stocked, and like all seasonal releases, once they're gone, these are likely gone for good (or at least until next spring).Nashville Hot-Style SausageCredit: Kimberly Holland/Southern LivingI'll be honest that what first caught my eye in the meat counter was another limited-edition meat: Pineapple Bacon Flavored Sausage. But then the vibrant color of these sausages drew me in. In my store, they were stocked just above the other, more traditional sausages, like Italian and chicken sausages, and come five to a pack so you can grill these up on their own, serve them in a bun with sauteed peppers and onions, or open slice them for a hot and spicy pasta alternative.Strawberry Lemonade Cake CookiesCredit: Kimberly Holland/Southern LivingBeyond the new cream cheese pies, Publix keeps things interesting in the bakery, too. Recently, I've seen all sorts of new things, not always labeled new or limited edition, including fried hand pies and guava pastries. But these Strawberry Lemonade Cake Cookies were too much fun to pass up as I was making my way to the dairy section. They were already down to just one one container, so you know these are bound to be popular.Read the original article on Southern Living",
